<title>AUSTRALIA: Plutonic shares strenghened by Q2 report.</title>
<headline>Plutonic shares strenghened by Q2 report.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in gold miner Plutonic Resources Ltd jumped over 5.3 percent to A$4.00 in active trade on Thursday as more investors bought in on the back of an impressive quarterly report.</p>
<p>Tuesday's quarterly announced record gold production of 138,231 ounces in the quarter ended June 30, while also reporting a sharp fall in operating costs.</p>
<p>&quot;Record production, cash costs coming down, it was a great quarterly,&quot; said dealer Justin Hondris, of Hartley Poynton.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks to be one of the most attractive golds out there.&quot;</p>
</text>
